<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:bioc="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn/biocolor/1.0" xmlns:color="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/non-normative/color/1.0" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_1ksue5u" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Camunda Modeler" exporterVersion="5.22.0" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.4.0">
  <bpmn:process id="Process_TourCreation" name="ACME_Picking_TourCreation" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Workflow 101: Batch tour creation for fulfillable picking orders.

Triggered by: Temporal Schedule (every 2h, overlap=SKIP) OR custom event mutation (manual).
Both use the same workflow code -- no input required.

Flow:
1. Query ALL picking orders where data.status=="fulfillable"
2. If 0 → complete immediately
3. Batch into groups of max 8 (configurable)
4. LOOP over each batch:
   a. Create one container repo per order (no parent, floating)
   b. For each order item: create item movement storage slot → container
   c. Create a movement collection (MC) with all movements for the batch
   d. Update each order: data.status="in_tour" (with optimistic check)
5. Return: list of MC IDs, total orders assigned

CONCURRENCY SAFETY:
- Temporal Schedule uses ScheduleOverlapPolicy=SKIP (prevents schedule+schedule overlap)
- Manual triggers can overlap with scheduled runs
- UpdateOrderStatus uses OPTIMISTIC CONCURRENCY CHECK: before setting "in_tour",
  verify current status is still "fulfillable". If already "in_tour" (claimed by
  concurrent run), skip the order silently. This prevents double-assignment.

MOVEMENT STRUCTURE:
  Each MC = one pick tour (up to 8 orders).
  MC contains item movements: storage slot → per-order container.
  Containers created with no parent (floating).
  In workflow 102: picker scans trolley, scans X containers,
  background job places containers onto trolley.

PARKED FOR LATER:
- Sort strategy for pick route optimization
- Partial fulfillment handling (workflow 102 responsibility)
- Container-to-outbound movement (workflow 102)</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Event_083gpo3" name="Scheduled&#10;(every 2h)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Temporal Schedule: runs every 2 hours.
ScheduleOverlapPolicy=SKIP prevents concurrent scheduled runs.
Does NOT prevent overlap with manual triggers — the optimistic
status check in UpdateOrderStatus handles that.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_0d1dpdy</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:timerEventDefinition id="TimerEventDefinition_0w9alie" />
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Event_09woa0g" name="Manual Trigger&#10;(custom event)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Custom event mutation via Pyck API.
Can overlap with scheduled runs — safe due to optimistic status check.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1o0hl68</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_0d1dpdy" sourceRef="Event_083gpo3" targetRef="Activity_1ojjtgp" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_1ojjtgp" name="Fetch ALL fulfillable orders">
      <bpmn:documentation>Activity: FetchFulfillableOrders

Query: ALL pickingOrders where data.status=="fulfillable".
Uses cursor-based pagination to handle large result sets.
If 0 orders → workflow completes immediately.

NOTE: Sort strategy parked for later.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_0d1dpdy</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1o0hl68</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_fetch_to_routetable</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1o0hl68" sourceRef="Event_09woa0g" targetRef="Activity_1ojjtgp" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_fetch_to_routetable" sourceRef="Activity_1ojjtgp" targetRef="Activity_fetch_route_table" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_fetch_route_table" name="Fetch route table (Z2 walkways, depot, dropoff)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Activity: FetchRouteTable

Loads the Z2 routing master data: walkway geometry per aisle,
aisle→walkway mapping, depot + dropoff anchors. Loud failure on
missing/duplicate routing rows — tours must not be planned on a
broken route table. (Added to the diagram in the 2026-06-10 sync;
the route-planning era activities were missing here.)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_fetch_to_routetable</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_routetable_to_picklocs</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_routetable_to_picklocs" sourceRef="Activity_fetch_route_table" targetRef="Activity_fetch_pick_locations" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_fetch_pick_locations" name="Resolve pick locations + skip unfulfillable + sort by centroid">
      <bpmn:documentation>Activity: FetchPickLocations (+ in-workflow annotate/skip/sort)

Aggregates per-SKU demand ACROSS the fetched orders, resolves one
slot per SKU from live NET stock (latest stock row; reservations
excluded; nearest-to-depot tiebreak by name asc).

In-workflow follow-ups (no separate activities):
- Orders containing any unfulfillable item are SKIPPED — they stay
  "fulfillable" and the next scheduled run retries them (no
  escalation step yet).
- Remaining orders are sorted by pick-centroid (route.SortOrdersByCentroid)
  before batching, so each tour's picks cluster spatially.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_routetable_to_picklocs</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_to_gateway</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_batches" name="Batches&#10;remaining?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_to_gateway</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_loop_back</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_yes_batch</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_no_batch</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_to_gateway" sourceRef="Activity_fetch_pick_locations" targetRef="Gateway_batches" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_create_tour" name="Create tour for next batch (max 8 orders)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Activity: CreateTour (called once per batch)

For each order in the batch:
1. Create container repo (acme-container, no parent)
2. For each order item: movement from first Z2 storage slot → container
3. Create MC (acme-movement-collection) with all movements

MC creation fires inventory.collection-movement.create → triggers wf102.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_yes_batch</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_to_update</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_yes_batch" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gateway_batches" targetRef="Activity_create_tour" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_update_status" name="Update orders → in_tour (optimistic check)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Activity: UpdateOrderStatus (called once per order in the batch)

OPTIMISTIC CONCURRENCY:
1. Fetch current order data
2. Check data.status is still "fulfillable"
   - If "fulfillable" → set to "in_tour" + statusAt=now
   - If already "in_tour" or beyond → SKIP (concurrent run claimed it)
3. Returns {skipped: true/false}

This prevents double-assignment when manual and scheduled runs overlap.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_to_update</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_loop_back</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_to_update" sourceRef="Activity_create_tour" targetRef="Activity_update_status" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_loop_back" sourceRef="Activity_update_status" targetRef="Gateway_batches" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_0ruyaxs" name="All tours created">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_no_batch</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_no_batch" name="No" sourceRef="Gateway_batches" targetRef="Event_0ruyaxs" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_fetch">
      <bpmn:text>Fetches ALL fulfillable orders at once.
50 orders → 7 batches processed in this loop.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Association_fetch" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Activity_1ojjtgp" targetRef="TextAnnotation_fetch" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_tour">
      <bpmn:text>Max 8 orders/MC (configurable).
Creates: 1 container/order, N movements, 1 MC.
Containers: no parent (placed on trolley in wf102).</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Association_tour" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Activity_create_tour" targetRef="TextAnnotation_tour" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_optimistic">
      <bpmn:text>OPTIMISTIC CHECK: skip if order already claimed
by a concurrent run (status != "fulfillable").</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Association_optimistic" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Activity_update_status" targetRef="TextAnnotation_optimistic" />
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_1">
